ecause `g_pow43[144] == 16 * g_pow43[32]` bit-exactly in `f32`; the `2/9` literal substitution uses a genuinely different `f32` yet never changes `poly` for any `x` (verified exhaustively over 2³¹).\n\nOne caveat on the reference itself: the C diverges from its own baseline build by 24 values under `-march=x86-64-v3` (FMA contraction) and 2082 under `-Ofast`. `CMakeLists.txt` sets no flags, so baseline is the correct target — and Rust matches it under every `target-cpu`, since it never auto-contracts.","ttft_ms":2737,"ttft_stream_ms":2577,"time_to_request_ms":45,"type":"result","duration_ms":2236483,"uuid":"1abbdcaf-0855-4c78-a95d-c5d1e8fef51a","queued_turn_count":0}
